# charon integration step 49 after 546078ea5d: commit 5d639e32bef8a61ea3dacd578be70df94269bb6c
# first parent 0c5f84430d9df46790daec9c555ad8fa4023d82f
# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: a switch without an exit takes the join of its branches, not a copy per path
#
# compute_switch_exits gives a switch an exit (a block whose code is emitted once, after the switch)
# only if its block with the highest flow is not taken and every path from the switch reaches it
# before any exit of an outer switch. After a `?`, whose switch takes the cleanup of the early
# returns as its exit, every later switch whose branches may return early reaches that exit without
# passing its own join: it gets no exit, and ReconstructMode::Duplicate copies everything after the
# join into every branch path, multiplied by the nested and following switches that fail the same
# way. `let a = g(0)?; for op in ops { let v = match op { A => g(1)?, .. }; acc += tail(v); }` had
# one copy of `acc += tail(v)` per arm, 16 with nested `if`s, and in the core
# chelis_ir::eval::eval_tensor_internal_with_result_claims got a 265 MB LLBC body (the whole
# chelis-types and chelis-ir crates did not fit in 12 GB).
#
# A switch that gets no exit this way now takes the best join of at least two of its branches, if
# the paths from the switch that avoid the join and stay inside the current loop reach no exit of an
# outer switch other than an exit cleanup, and if the code after the join (inside the loop, exit
# cleanups excluded) is larger than the largest such cleanup, which these paths then get a copy of.
# An exit cleanup (BlockData::exit_cleanup_size) is a block of storage markers and drops on a
# straight path to a `return` or to the next iteration of a loop: the early returns of a function
# and the `continue`s of a loop share them, they have the highest flow, and they are never a join.
# all_paths_go_through takes a target predicate and an optional loop to stay in. Switches that the
# first rule gives an exit keep it.
#
# The choice of exits does not change the meaning of the LLBC: only the innermost switch exit is
# reached by falling through, any other jump to an exit is translated in place.
#
# Test: control-flow/switch-exits-after-early-return (one call of `tail` per function; before: 4
# after a `?` and a loop, 16 with nested `if`s, 4 after a `?` without loop, 4 with a step dispatch
# that continues after a `?`).

